knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3734
What it fixes: vinext's `/_next/image` handler never sent `x-nextjs-cache`. Next.js sends it
on every successful image response (next-server.ts selects MISS/HIT/STALE,
image-optimizer.ts setResponseHeaders writes it), and Next's own og-api e2e asserts
`x-nextjs-cache: MISS` on the first optimized request. vinext keeps no image cache, so
every 200 it builds is a MISS; the header is set where the other image security headers are,
which covers the transformed, passthrough and SVG-passthrough paths and leaves 400/404 bare.
In a Nitro production build that handler is never reached: the App Router handler answers
`/_next/image` with a 302 to the source asset (app-rsc-handler.js), so the response a client
sees comes from Nitro's static handler. When Nitro's app is on globalThis.__nitro__.default the
handler now serves the image itself through handleNitroImageOptimization, which follows Next.js:
the source request carries no client headers, only Content-Type/Content-Length/ETag/
Last-Modified/Cache-Control are kept from the source (never Set-Cookie), non-image sources are
rejected, and Cache-Control is `public, max-age=<max(source max-age, 14400)>, must-revalidate`
(immutable only for hashed /_next/static/media sources). Dev keeps the redirect.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3734.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

